            new("Prepare your interview setup", "Test the meeting application, microphone, camera and internet connection before the scheduled time. Choose a space where you can hear clearly and limit interruptions, and tell others when you need quiet. Keep the invitation and recruiter contact accessible in case the connection fails. Use a professional display name and close unrelated windows before sharing your screen. You do not need an elaborate background; prioritize clear sound and a workable connection. If you need an accommodation or alternative format, discuss it with the recruiter in advance. Have your resume available for reference."),
            new("Show evidence of independent work", "Prepare an example of planning a task, breaking it into steps and checking progress without constant supervision. Explain how you handled a blocker and when you asked for help. For a technical role, show how you recorded a problem so another person could reproduce it. For an operational role, describe how you kept records accurate and priorities visible. Practise writing a brief update stating what is complete, what remains and what decision you need. Adapt examples to the responsibilities advertised. Explain how you would communicate a delay early enough for others to respond."),
            new("Behave thoughtfully on calls", "Join on time, greet the interviewer and check that you can hear each other. Allow a short pause before responding if the connection has a delay. Listen without multitasking and explain if you need a moment to locate a document. If audio fails, state the problem calmly through the available channel instead of repeatedly speaking over the other person. Avoid showing private messages or documents during screen sharing. Be honest about availability and working conditions, and ask how the team handles urgent requests outside normal hours. Keep your answers clear and focused."),
            new("Clarify how the team works", "Ask how tasks are assigned, how progress is reviewed and which communication channels serve different needs. Discuss onboarding, training and access to help for new joiners. Clarify whether performance is assessed through agreed outcomes, scheduled coverage or another approach. If selected, establish a routine for focused work, breaks and updates that fits the agreed schedule. Keep work information in approved systems and follow the employer's access instructions. Review written terms before assuming flexibility means working from any location at any time. Agree on how you will notify the team about unexpected interruptions.")
