            new("Revise through practical examples", "Select a laboratory exercise or project illustrating a relevant principle. Explain the objective, assumptions, method and observations before describing the conclusion. Be prepared to discuss units, measurement limits and why a result might differ from an expected value. Review relevant diagrams, calculations or drawings you have used. If software was involved, explain the inputs and how you checked the output rather than treating the tool as proof of correctness. Acknowledge where a classroom exercise differs from a real production or site environment. Keep project evidence organized so you can explain it clearly."),
            new("Prepare for technical questions", "Practise breaking an unfamiliar problem into known facts, missing information and a possible first step. Explain why you would choose a calculation, inspection or test before proposing a change. For maintenance scenarios, focus on gathering evidence and following authorized procedures rather than guessing at a repair. For design work, discuss constraints and how you would compare alternatives. Keep examples within your experience and say when you would consult a qualified supervisor. Prepare to explain a failed experiment and what it taught you about checking assumptions. Listen for additional conditions before finalizing an answer."),
