            new("Practise clear communication", "Prepare a brief introduction in the language required for the role. Speak at a steady pace and use simple words that make your message easy to follow. For email or chat, practise writing a response that acknowledges the issue, asks one useful question and explains the next step. Proofread names, dates and instructions before sending. For voice work, practise listening to a short scenario and summarizing it accurately. Avoid putting on an unfamiliar accent or using elaborate phrases that obscure your meaning. Ask a practice partner whether your explanation was easy to understand."),
            new("Work through customer scenarios", "Ask a friend to describe a problem with incomplete information, then practise clarifying it without making the person repeat everything. Confirm what you understand before suggesting an action. Explain what you would check, what you can do yourself and when you would escalate through the team's process. If you do not know an answer, say you would verify it rather than inventing a promise. Prepare an example of handling feedback or resolving a misunderstanding. Connect it to patience, accuracy and follow-through instead of claiming you never make mistakes. Keep the customer's objective in mind."),
            new("Behave calmly during the interview", "Greet the interviewer politely, listen without interrupting and answer directly. In a role-play, acknowledge frustration without blaming the customer or another colleague. Avoid arguing, making personal remarks or promising an outcome beyond your authority. If the interviewer changes the scenario, adapt your response instead of forcing a memorized script. Keep a professional tone when challenged and ask for clarification if needed. Be candid about shift availability and language skills so a successful interview leads to a role you can realistically perform. Pause briefly when necessary rather than filling every silence with an answer."),
